The Reto Pano uses masks.
The Reto Pano allows light to hit a full 3:2 area of the film roll in standard mode.
In panoramic mode, masks on the top and bottom of the Reto Pano's frame move down.
These masks block light from hitting the top and bottom areas of the film strip in panoramic mode.
In panoramic mode, the Reto Pano exposes only the middle of the film strip.
The Reto Pano exposes for a little more than half of the total space a typical photo would in panoramic mode.
